    "answer": {
      "short": "$A=-\\frac12$, $n=2$, $c=\\frac12$.\n\nThe software graphs coincide: $\\sin^2x=-\\frac12\\cos(2x)+\\frac12$.",
      "worked": "The software graph of $y=\\sin^2x$ has minimum $0$, maximum $1$ and period $\\pi$. Its midline is $y=\\frac12$ and its amplitude is $\\frac12$.\n\nChoose $c=\\frac12$ to set the midline and $n=2$ to give period $\\pi$. Since the graph has a minimum at $x=0$, choose $A=-\\frac12$.\n\nPlot $y=-\\frac12\\cos(2x)+\\frac12$ on the same axes as $y=\\sin^2x$. The curves coincide, including the minima at $x=0,\\pi,2\\pi$ and maxima at $x=\\frac\\pi2,\\frac{3\\pi}2$.",
